${U}_{\mathrm{surface}} + {E}_{1} = {U}_{h} KE$ of satellite is zero at earth surface and at height $h - \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{{R}_{e}} + {E}_{1} = - \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} {E}_{1} = G{M}_{e}m\left(\frac{1}{{R}_{e}} - \frac{1}{{R}_{e} + h}\right) {E}_{1} = \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} \times \frac{h}{{R}_{e}}$

Gravitational attraction ${F}_{G} = m{a}_{C} = \frac{m{v}^{2}}{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} \implies \frac{m{v}^{2}}{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} = \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)}^{2}} m{v}^{2} = \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} {E}_{2} = \frac{m{v}^{2}}{2} = \frac{G{M}_{e}m}{2\left({R}_{e} + h\right)} {E}_{1} = {E}_{2} \frac{h}{{R}_{e}} = \frac{1}{2} \implies h = \frac{{R}_{e}}{2} = 3200\mathrm{km}$

